<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30532" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγχᾰλῑνόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>put a bit in the mouth of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					76.14
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ στόματα ἐγκεχαλινωμένους</span>
			<i>having the bit in</i> their mouths, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.14
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.2.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.117
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δῆμον ἐγκεχαλινωμένον τῇ
				ὀλιγαρχία</span>
			<i>held in check</i> by the oligarchy, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργή -ωμένη τῷ λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					17.214d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph. of
			reins, <i>to be in the form of a bit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Oss.</u>
				19
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
